WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.785 --> 01:30.705
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.624 --> 01:33.959
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.835 --> 01:35.878
Black Jack.

01:48.865 --> 01:52.075
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "The Phoenix”

01:48.865 --> 01:52.075
Legend of the Phoenix

02:01.210 --> 02:04.337
Doc, it's a package sent via international mail.

02:05.882 --> 02:07.048
From who?

02:09.677 --> 02:11.762
There is no sender's address.

02:14.599 --> 02:15.766
What's that?

02:15.892 --> 02:17.100
It's a CD-ROM.

02:20.938 --> 02:22.272
It's voice data.

02:23.649 --> 02:25.233
Looks like there's no virus.

02:26.550 --> 02:27.750
Dr. Black Jack,

02:28.136 --> 02:30.733
one of my family members is suffering
from a severe illness.

02:31.280 --> 02:35.588
We will pay you in excess of 10,000,000 dollars.

02:37.704 --> 02:40.749
How much is 10,000,000 dollars?

02:41.167 --> 02:44.669
We have nobody to turn to but you, Dr. Black Jack.

02:45.171 --> 02:47.339
The patient is a 200-year-old man.

02:48.925 --> 02:51.760
Please help us.

02:53.262 --> 02:54.304
Impossible!

02:54.507 --> 02:56.515
What's wrong, Doc?

02:56.849 --> 02:59.142
It must be some sort of prank.

02:59.560 --> 03:01.978
There is no way it could be a 200-year-old man.

03:02.480 --> 03:03.690
Really?

03:04.649 --> 03:07.584
At most, people can live for 120 years or so.

03:07.777 --> 03:11.530
So you're not going to go see this patient?

03:11.989 --> 03:15.075
There is no way a 200-year-old patient exists.

03:15.076 --> 03:18.279
Besides, I have other patients right now.

03:25.128 --> 03:29.923
I believe a successful surgical treatment of cerebral
softening caused by old age is unprecedented.

03:30.633 --> 03:32.634
I suppose medication is not effective either.

03:33.010 --> 03:36.721
Dr. Asano is our teacher, but he is old.

03:37.265 --> 03:39.808
He is in the same age category as Dr. Honma.

03:40.727 --> 03:41.893
It's not possible...

03:44.731 --> 03:45.689
Sorry.

03:46.399 --> 03:47.524
It's fine.

03:47.525 --> 03:51.688
It's true that I couldn't save Dr. Honma that day.

03:55.408 --> 03:57.409
Dr. Honma saved my life.

03:58.703 --> 04:02.664
I really wanted him to get better,
but the surgery was useless.

04:08.629 --> 04:11.190
It's impossible with the current technology.

04:15.011 --> 04:18.597
We have nobody to turn to but you, Dr. Black Jack.

04:18.931 --> 04:20.974
The patient is a 200-year-old man.

04:21.976 --> 04:24.311
The patient is a 200-year-old man.

04:24.562 --> 04:27.213
Please help us.

04:43.081 --> 04:45.665
It's a long journey from Japan,

04:45.666 --> 04:49.628
but if you come to the nearby airport, we will pick you up.

04:50.296 --> 04:52.547
Can I have some mixed juice?

04:53.091 --> 04:54.132
Sure.

04:56.010 --> 04:57.295
Here you go.

05:01.474 --> 05:03.725
This is such a nice trip.

05:04.185 --> 05:06.937
It probably won't be like this for long.

05:43.474 --> 05:46.727
We've come to an incredibly faraway land.

05:48.020 --> 05:48.930
Now...

05:52.734 --> 05:54.276
Dr. Black Jack, right?

05:54.318 --> 05:54.981
Yes.

05:59.240 --> 06:00.322
I'm Miriam.

06:00.742 --> 06:02.534
I appreciate you coming.

06:04.078 --> 06:05.620
I am...

06:05.663 --> 06:09.416
Doc's wife, Pinoco.

06:10.042 --> 06:11.162
Wife?

06:21.971 --> 06:22.840
What's that?

06:24.015 --> 06:25.348
Oh, that?

06:25.975 --> 06:27.309
It's a stun gun.

06:27.310 --> 06:28.937
What do you need that for?

06:29.228 --> 06:30.687
You'll see later.

06:36.819 --> 06:38.779
It's like a picnic.

06:39.197 --> 06:40.864
Here, Doc.

06:42.325 --> 06:44.910
We cant do this for long.

06:53.294 --> 06:55.921
This is quite a place.

06:55.922 --> 06:59.925
I didn't think such incredible scenery still existed on Earth.

06:59.926 --> 07:02.550
There used to be more nomads.

07:02.845 --> 07:04.119
Where did they go?

07:04.347 --> 07:05.931
Off to cities.

07:06.516 --> 07:10.185
You said you will pay 10,000,000 dollars.

07:10.186 --> 07:10.894
How are you going to pay?

07:11.729 --> 07:14.064
It's a payment that's worth 10,000,000 dollars.

07:15.858 --> 07:17.651
Did you find some jewelry or something?

07:18.069 --> 07:20.386
It's worth far more.

07:20.822 --> 07:24.116
200-year-old man, must be some kind of mistake.

07:24.534 --> 07:26.076
See him for yourself.

07:27.370 --> 07:28.954
Doc, look.

07:31.249 --> 07:32.360
That's an ovoo.

07:32.667 --> 07:36.920
They're road signs that the nomads built all over the place.

08:04.532 --> 08:06.950
Here we are.

08:07.160 --> 08:10.454
Ohmigewdness...

08:15.209 --> 08:17.071
Here, please come in.

08:23.009 --> 08:26.219
Doc, what's that?

08:31.350 --> 08:32.546
This is...

08:33.895 --> 08:36.625
What a sight!

08:38.274 --> 08:40.150
This patient is that old man.

08:40.610 --> 08:43.411
He is my great-great-great-great-grandfather.

08:43.905 --> 08:46.905
He's looked like that ever since I was a child.

08:47.325 --> 08:48.921
He turns 200 years old this year.

08:49.494 --> 08:51.789
You don't have his birth records, do you?

08:52.497 --> 08:53.690
It's some kind of mistake.

08:54.373 --> 08:57.399
More precisely, he's 199 years and 3 months old.

08:57.627 --> 09:01.409
There is a record that says he was born in the same
year as the great flood that hit this region.

09:03.341 --> 09:07.923
I've heard that there have been many reports of
longevity between the Caucasus and West Asia,

09:08.387 --> 09:10.055
but never 200 years.

09:10.640 --> 09:13.642
There is a legend of a phoenix in this area.

09:14.185 --> 09:15.931
What's a phoenix?

09:16.354 --> 09:18.557
The phoenix is a bird that never dies.

09:19.190 --> 09:22.691
And people who drink its blood can live forever too.

09:23.277 --> 09:25.195
That's only a fairy tale.

09:25.571 --> 09:30.367
The reason he can't die is because he drank its blood.

09:30.368 --> 09:31.159
Impossible!

09:31.411 --> 09:35.080
Then how could he live for 200 years?

09:35.456 --> 09:38.203
There must be some scientific reason.

09:38.459 --> 09:40.085
I don't believe this phoenix exists.

09:43.714 --> 09:45.972
Then I will prove it to you.

09:52.432 --> 09:54.266
Doc,

09:54.267 --> 09:56.393
wait.

09:56.644 --> 09:57.815
Wait.

10:01.858 --> 10:03.317
Where are the other villagers?

10:03.609 --> 10:07.237
They said that it was too remote
here, so they moved to cities.

10:07.822 --> 10:10.115
Why won't you move?

10:10.491 --> 10:13.180
And leave behind the land that
was passed on for generations?

10:13.453 --> 10:15.251
How could I do that?

10:16.414 --> 10:20.375
The phoenix belongs to the people who protect this land.

10:24.046 --> 10:29.259
By luck, Grandfather found and cut the
phoenix with a knife when he was young.

10:29.552 --> 10:31.386
The phoenix got away,

10:31.387 --> 10:35.600
but he licked the blood that was on the
knife, and obtained eternal life.

10:35.808 --> 10:37.413
But he did get sick.

10:37.685 --> 10:38.560
Yes.

10:38.561 --> 10:40.645
He gets old, and gets sick too.

10:41.731 --> 10:44.399
He may suffer from illness, but he never dies.

10:47.195 --> 10:48.820
Look, that's it.

10:50.490 --> 10:52.632
That cave is the phoenix's nest.

11:02.794 --> 11:05.087
It's phoefenix!

11:05.505 --> 11:07.339
This is shocking.

11:07.924 --> 11:09.604
I've never seen such a glow.

11:09.801 --> 11:12.010
See? You find it mysterious too, right?

11:12.261 --> 11:13.044
Yeah.

11:13.471 --> 11:14.499
Look below.

11:15.223 --> 11:18.059
Inside the caves is a complex maze.

11:18.351 --> 11:20.404
Only Grandfather knows the way.

11:21.020 --> 11:25.459
He said he would show his family the path, but he got sick.

11:26.401 --> 11:28.995
Please, cure his illness.

11:29.195 --> 11:31.405
I want him to be able to talk again.

11:31.739 --> 11:34.199
And you will hear about the path from him,

11:34.200 --> 11:36.701
then shoot the phoenix with the stun gun.

11:37.620 --> 11:40.455
It's a payment that's worth more than 10,000,000 dollars.

11:42.818 --> 11:46.169
Grandfather could live for 200
years just from one lick of it.

11:46.712 --> 11:48.616
Then what if I drink a spoonful?

11:48.840 --> 11:50.924
Or a glass of its blood?

11:50.925 --> 11:53.557
Would it give you eternal youth?

11:53.886 --> 11:55.095
I don't know.

11:55.930 --> 12:01.059
You've taken large sums of money from
many rich people to cure them, right?

12:02.937 --> 12:10.569
How much would they pay for eternal life, if they are willing
to pay a large sum just to extend their lives temporarily?

12:10.570 --> 12:13.447
You'd start a new business with the phoenix's blood?

12:13.656 --> 12:14.557
Yes.

12:14.907 --> 12:17.117
It will bring in millions.

12:35.001 --> 12:36.251
He has terminal symptoms.

12:36.252 --> 12:39.088
Sarcomas have spread all over the place,
and have grown too large in each spot.

12:39.464 --> 12:41.507
How could he survive like this?

12:41.549 --> 12:42.549
It's unbelievable.

12:43.260 --> 12:44.760
I told you so.

12:45.053 --> 12:47.304
He can't even die.

12:47.889 --> 12:52.184
Having spread this much, another one will come
back quickly even if we eliminate them now.

12:52.185 --> 12:53.227
It's useless.

12:53.687 --> 12:54.961
Just do it, please.

12:55.397 --> 12:56.689
Get rid of them all.

13:36.313 --> 13:39.988
The extraction is complete for now, but
the possibility of recurrence is high.

13:40.317 --> 13:41.810
He won't last like this.

13:42.235 --> 13:43.444
It's okay.

13:43.445 --> 13:45.362
He will continue to live.

13:45.905 --> 13:48.741
We just need to let him drink the phoenix's blood.

13:49.242 --> 13:51.702
I would love to ask this old man

13:52.245 --> 13:55.831
what it feels like to live for 200 years.

13:55.832 --> 13:58.459
Now, get me more water.

14:06.718 --> 14:07.751
Potty.

14:11.890 --> 14:13.390
You are...

14:15.685 --> 14:17.436
Can you talk now?

14:18.313 --> 14:20.648
Yeah, thanks to you.

14:21.274 --> 14:23.609
We'd better go to town and re-examine you.

14:23.860 --> 14:26.737
I'd like to check you out thoroughly, too.

14:27.322 --> 14:30.699
You saved my life, so let me be honest with you.

14:30.700 --> 14:33.035
I didn't drink the blood.

14:33.370 --> 14:37.262
That's a lie that I drank the bird's blood.

14:37.374 --> 14:38.123
What?

14:38.249 --> 14:43.087
It's true that we went to capture
the phoenix when I was young.

14:43.463 --> 14:47.132
I still remember it clearly.

14:49.261 --> 14:54.014
I searched the path with the
others after a hard day's work.

14:54.432 --> 14:58.978
I left a partial map under the ovoo.

15:00.563 --> 15:04.608
There is one spot that has a 5-way split,

15:04.609 --> 15:07.064
but the twin rocks will guide you.

15:07.362 --> 15:13.867
Go between the twin rocks, and the cave
in which the phoenix lives is nearby.

15:22.961 --> 15:27.506
We got that far, but we couldn't catch the phoenix.

15:27.924 --> 15:32.405
From my bitter disappointment,
I lied that I drank the blood.

15:32.637 --> 15:38.444
Eventually, people started treating
me better and better as I got older.

15:38.810 --> 15:41.757
They must have believed that it
was the power of the phoenix.

15:42.063 --> 15:45.482
But I was scared about what would happen
if they learned the truth about the lie.

15:46.318 --> 15:51.947
I wanted to make the lie the truth, so
I wouldn't be exiled from this land.

15:51.948 --> 15:58.996
I wished that I would drink the blood of the
phoenix someday to obtain eternal life.

15:58.997 --> 16:00.831
I lived on like that.

16:01.458 --> 16:02.875
So that's how - 200 years.

16:03.168 --> 16:05.377
I've lived so long.

16:05.378 --> 16:06.623
It's all about determination.

16:07.005 --> 16:09.644
But my children died, then my grandchildren died,

16:09.841 --> 16:13.344
and even my great-grandchildren and
great-great-grandchildren passed away, too.

16:14.012 --> 16:18.599
Tell her that I don't need the blood anymore.

16:19.017 --> 16:21.788
Miriam wants the blood of the phoenix.

16:22.145 --> 16:24.563
You must not get close to the phoenix.

16:25.523 --> 16:27.458
I'd love to know too.

16:27.901 --> 16:31.028
Does the blood that provides eternal life really exist?

16:32.030 --> 16:33.338
You must not!

16:34.532 --> 16:39.495
Doc, that woman ran off toward
the mountain with her gun.

16:40.038 --> 16:40.978
No!

16:41.706 --> 16:42.873
In that cave...

16:47.170 --> 16:49.296
there are vipers!

16:53.426 --> 16:55.177
Pinoco, look after the man!

16:55.470 --> 16:56.625
Me?

17:01.685 --> 17:02.394
Ovoo!

17:02.644 --> 17:03.602
This must be it.

17:22.372 --> 17:24.832
Hey! Stop!

17:29.879 --> 17:32.543
Doctor, it's too late now.

17:37.262 --> 17:38.304
Hey!

17:38.763 --> 17:39.638
It's me!

17:40.265 --> 17:41.473
Don't get close to the bird!

17:42.142 --> 17:44.280
There are vipers ahead!

17:57.490 --> 18:01.368
<i>I must take it down in one shot, or it will be gone forever.</i>

18:10.837 --> 18:11.920
Yes!

18:11.921 --> 18:12.838
I did it!

18:29.105 --> 18:29.896
Hey!

18:30.482 --> 18:32.149
Doctor, help me!

18:33.762 --> 18:34.443
Wait there!

18:42.410 --> 18:44.217
Hey, hang in there!

18:47.165 --> 18:48.447
The vipers are glowing too.

18:49.960 --> 18:52.127
It's the same glow as the phoenix.

18:54.839 --> 18:55.965
Blood...

18:57.342 --> 18:58.467
Blood...

18:59.594 --> 19:01.679
It's the luminescent bacteria.

19:02.138 --> 19:04.994
If I drink the phoenix's blood...

19:07.352 --> 19:08.310
Stop it!

19:08.311 --> 19:12.648
Both the bird and the snakes are just
covered by luminescent bacteria!

19:13.275 --> 19:15.109
Drinking its blood won't save you!

19:15.652 --> 19:17.278
That's not...

19:18.697 --> 19:19.905
true.

19:22.575 --> 19:23.453
Come back!

19:23.660 --> 19:24.868
I must apply first aid!

19:31.376 --> 19:32.085
Hey!

19:33.628 --> 19:35.100
Hang in there, Miriam.

19:38.341 --> 19:40.609
W... why?

19:42.053 --> 19:42.720
Hey, Miriam!

19:58.111 --> 20:00.613
Hang in there.

20:00.864 --> 20:02.534
There will be some serum in town.

20:03.116 --> 20:03.824
She'll be fine.

20:15.337 --> 20:16.045
What's this?

20:17.088 --> 20:19.590
It's the components of that bird's blood.

20:20.258 --> 20:21.967
It was on your hand.

20:22.677 --> 20:25.012
I took it as you promised.

20:26.389 --> 20:28.234
There is nothing special.

20:28.475 --> 20:30.225
It's no different from any other bird's.

20:30.226 --> 20:31.903
No! That's a lie!

20:32.270 --> 20:35.230
There must be some power that cannot
be detected by the exam!

20:35.982 --> 20:37.656
That's not the phoenix.

20:38.068 --> 20:40.069
It looked like it was glowing because of the bacteria.

20:40.070 --> 20:41.070
It's just an ordinary bird.

20:41.193 --> 20:44.323
Then why is there a phoenix legend?

20:44.324 --> 20:47.281
There must be a real phoenix somewhere!

20:48.286 --> 20:50.913
Doc, I bought this!

20:51.039 --> 20:53.374
It's a souvenir for Sharaku.

20:55.418 --> 20:57.920
It's okay to believe in legends.

20:58.463 --> 21:01.861
But don't you think it's foolish to
lose your life because of them?

21:02.509 --> 21:04.241
There is no eternal life.

21:21.569 --> 21:23.742
I'd like some mixed juice.

21:23.989 --> 21:25.364
Here you go.

21:28.952 --> 21:32.830
I'd much prefer this over the phoenix's blood.

21:36.126 --> 21:37.809
Doc, there!

21:38.712 --> 21:39.670
What?

21:40.922 --> 21:41.880
Oh?

21:42.215 --> 21:44.216
It's nothing.

21:45.594 --> 21:48.498
Doc, don't you want the phoenix's blood?

21:48.930 --> 21:52.182
My job is not to make people immortal.

21:52.934 --> 21:54.599
It's to cure them.

22:07.077 --> 22:19.032
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.077 --> 22:19.032
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.150 --> 22:24.149
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.150 --> 22:24.149
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.718 --> 22:31.187
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.718 --> 22:31.187
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.731 --> 22:37.189
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.731 --> 22:37.189
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.793 --> 22:40.278
being heated up by you,

22:37.793 --> 22:40.278
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.487 --> 22:48.264
so much that I change color

22:40.487 --> 22:48.264
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.349 --> 23:00.118
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.349 --> 23:00.118
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.326 --> 23:12.057
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.326 --> 23:12.057
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.297 --> 23:23.648
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.297 --> 23:23.648
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.834 --> 23:28.755
I couldn't be happier

23:23.834 --> 23:28.755
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:28.983 --> 23:33.917
How does it taste?

23:28.983 --> 23:33.916
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.053 --> 24:15.068
The Gift From a Killer Whale

23:45.308 --> 23:46.755
What's this?

23:51.195 --> 23:55.328
We fishermen always coexisted with them.

23:55.967 --> 23:57.596
Kill the man-eating whale!

24:05.456 --> 24:06.823
I won't let you die!

24:10.373 --> 24:13.286
Next Karte - The Gift From a Killer Whale.

24:15.843 --> 24:17.760
Pinoco's Diary...

24:18.511 --> 24:21.778
My job is not to make people immortal.

24:22.358 --> 24:23.798
It's to cure them.
